{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/769021-adopt-the-beast-shape-homebrew-abilities","id":769021,"title":"Adopt the Beast-Shape [Homebrew Abilities]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-19T00:26:49-08:00","id":769021,"title":"Adopt the Beast-Shape [Homebrew Abilities]","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Begotten may physically transform into the Beast her Soul reflects. She can call upon her Soul, letting it shift her body into a new, more powerful shape. In her bestial form, she may call upon one ability from the following list per dot of Lair she possesses, though she is not required to do so. Some Beasts find perfection with fewer abilities and never bother to grow this aspect of their Myth further. </div> </div> </div><b>- From Beast: The Primordial Kickstarter</b><br /> <br /> That said, we know that an Apex Beast can fly, develop natural armor, turn people to stone with its gaze, and/or any other assortment of powers available to those Begotten who attain the Incarnate Inheritance. Are there any other possible abilities that such powerful entities can develop? If you happen to have any thought up, feel free to post them down here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-categ